From 13e424a27c018679a1f2badcf4a47dbe2a2272fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hero <caleb@calebgj.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:10:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] lsa: the index ops at decode latency

Each op was a single workgroup's latency: a load at a time. The index
projection issues 32 of its map's loads ahead of its chain (63 -> 17 us a
decode row, 5.8 -> 0.55 ms a 8192-row chunk); Ward's search runs four
partners' dot products at once (809 -> 221 us a block); the select's pick
runs at 1024 threads with its scans four loads ahead, a three-digit radix
select (11/11/10 bits), members read 16 bytes at a time, and, given a
scratch, the first digit counted by the scoring launch across the device
(373 -> 135 us a decode row at 512k, 394 -> 100 us at 128k; R9700, top_k
4096, top_p 1024). Every order the arithmetic fixes is kept: the emulator and
the card still equal libref/ref_lsa.h to the bit, with and without the
scratch.

(cherry picked from commit 1c4a36c702fb5876c3622802fb91c83ab44f0c71)
