+`nsel` its length. libr4d's `lsa_select_i32` is two launches: a thread a bucket scores into `score`,
+then a workgroup of 1024 a row finds the `top_p`-th best by a three-digit radix select over the
+scores' order keys (11, 11 and 10 bits), sorts the candidates best first by a key no two share, cuts
+the walk by a prefix count and sorts the expansion. Given its scratch (`[M][2048]` u32) the scoring
+launch also counts the first digit across the device, which the pick would otherwise count alone; the
+result is the same either way. On an R9700 one decode row takes ~100 us at 128k of context and
+~135 us at 512k, the flat design's budget.
 
